 "summary": "The theorem says that for every finite-order ray class character χ of ℤ[ω] (trivial on units) and every s with Re s > 7/8, other than s = 1 when χ is principal, the function LFunction χ s is nonzero. LFunction is not defined by an Euler product or Dirichlet series over ideals. It is built from products of Hurwitz even kernels (theta series) through Mathlib's WeakFEPair.Λ. The main caveat is that nothing in the file shows this construction equals the Hecke L-function. The Dirichlet and ζ part of the paper's theorem is also not stated.",
 "glossary": [
  {"decl": "OAI.SevenEighths.HeckeFamily.K / O", "line": 208, "plain": "K = ℚ(ζ₃) = ℚ(√-3) and O = its ring of integers ℤ[ω].", "standard_concept": "F = ℚ(√-3) and 𝒪_F", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": ""},
  {"decl": "OAI.SevenEighths.HeckeFamily.Character", "line": 217, "plain": "A nonzero ideal m of O, a multiplicative character of (O/m) into ℂ that is trivial on the images of the units, and a positive integer N with N ∈ m.", "standard_concept": "Finite-order Hecke (ray class) character of Q(√-3) with modulus m", "matches_standard": "partly", "note": "Since the class number is 1 and the infinite place is complex, finite-order ray class characters correspond to characters of (O/m)^× trivial on units, so this looks right. The 'period' is extra data (some N ∈ m, which exists for any nonzero m). The modulus m = ⊤ (trivial ring) is allowed, giving the Dedekind zeta function of F."},
  {"decl": "OAI.SevenEighths.HeckeFamily.coefficients", "line": 230, "plain": "For (x,y) ∈ (Fin N)², the coefficient is χ(x + yω), which is 0 when x + yω is a nonunit mod m.", "standard_concept": "Coefficient of the character extended by zero on non-coprime residues", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": ""},
  {"decl": "OAI.SevenEighths.HeckeTheta.pair / completed / latticeL", "line": 194, "plain": "A weighted sum of rectangular products of Hurwitz even-kernel pairs, with shifts xShift, yShift and scalings L² and 3L², over residues mod N and parity e ∈ {0,1}. 'completed' is its Mellin-type Λ from Mathlib's WeakFEPair. latticeL s = π^s Γ(s)⁻¹ Λ(s).", "standard_concept": "Theta-series representation of the completed Hecke L-function Σ χ(a) N(a)^{-s} over the Eisenstein lattice", "matches_standard": "unclear", "note": "Nothing in the file shows that this equals the Dirichlet series Σ_{n≠0} χ(n)/(x²-xy+y²)^s (or the sum over ideals) for Re s > 1. The correctness of the shifts, the scalings L² and 3L², and the parity split cannot be checked from the statement."},
  {"decl": "OAI.SevenEighths.HeckeFamily.LFunction", "line": 235, "plain": "LFunction χ s = π^s · Γ(s)⁻¹ · Λ_pair(s) / 6.", "standard_concept": "Hecke L-function L(s,χ) = Σ_{ideals a} χ(a) N(a)^{-s} and its meromorphic continuation", "matches_standard": "unclear", "note": "The division by 6 matches |O^×| = 6 and is a nonzero scalar. The identification with the Hecke L-function is not established in the file. Mathlib's Λ is totalized at s = 0 and s = 1."}
 ],
 "lean_claims": [
  {"theorem": "OAI.SevenEighths.HeckeFamily.LFunction_ne_zero_of_seven_eighths_lt_re", "line": 237, "plain": "For every Character χ (ideal m, unit-trivial multiplicative character mod m, period N) and every complex s with Re s > 7/8, if not (χ.residue = 1 and s = 1), then LFunction χ s ≠ 0. Here LFunction χ s = π^s Γ(s)⁻¹ Λ(s)/6 for the theta-series pair attached to the coefficients χ(x+yω)."}
 ],
 "paper_claims": [
  {"ref": "Theorem 1.1 (thm:main), part 1", "plain": "Every finite-order Hecke L-function over Q(√-3) has no zero in Re s > 7/8."},
  {"ref": "Theorem 1.1, part 2", "plain": "The same holds for every Dirichlet L-function, including ζ(s)."},
  {"ref": "Theorem 1.1, part 3", "plain": "A pole at s = 1 for a principal character is allowed (it is not a zero)."}
 ],
